WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.840
John Rambo has been fighting his battles on
the big screen for nearly four decades.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.041
And now, we’re going to take a look at his
tale, from First Blood to Last Blood, and

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.000
explain his action-packed story.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.560
What little we know of John Rambo's early
life is cobbled together from various references

00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:18.590
he and other characters have made to it over
the course of the four films so far.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.310
He grew up on his dad's horse ranch, then
was drafted into the U.S. Army at the age

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.310
of 18.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.300
After nine months of training, he was deployed
to Vietnam, where he learned how to be really

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.119
good at killing, and how to tie a wicked headband.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:34.219
Rambo became a Green Beret and continued working
in deep cover and reconnaissance missions

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:38.670
until he was captured by the Viet Cong after
an ambush and became a prisoner of war.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.629
For the next several months, he was tortured
along with his comrades from Baker Team.

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:45.309
Fortunately, Rambo managed to escape the POW
camp.

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:49.260
He returned to military service, but the deep
trauma he'd suffered began to show through

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.640
in the form of a nervous breakdown, leading
to him eventually being honorably discharged.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:59.360
In December 1981, Rambo traveled to Washington
State to visit Delmar Barry, a friend from

00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:03.690
Baker Team, only to be told by Barry's family
that he'd died as a result of Agent Orange

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:04.690
exposure.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.480
This made Rambo the last surviving member
of Baker Team.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.240
"Baker team, they're all dead sir."

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.520
"Not Delmar Barry.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.600
He made it."

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.520
"Barry's gone too sir."

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.080
Rambo moved on, and wandered into the nearby
town of Hope, where the local sheriff Will

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.380
Teasle tried to quickly usher him out of town
for fear that he'd cause trouble.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.100
Rambo, who was just looking for something
to eat, went back into Hope anyway, leading

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.430
Teasle to arrest him.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.790
Teasle's deputies began harassing and threatening
Rambo at the station.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.670
Using his Green Beret skills, Rambo fought
his way out of the station before making his

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.830
getaway on a stolen motorcycle.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:44.040
In the ensuing search, Teasle's deputy, Art
Galt, began firing at Rambo from a helicopter.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.110
Rambo retaliated by hurling a rock at the
chopper.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:50.180
As a result, the helicopter pilot lost control,
and Galt fell to his death.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.760
Yeah, it was self-defense, but now he was
wanted for killing a cop.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.040
Dismayed over the death of Galt, Rambo tried
to convince Teasle that it was accidental,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.180
and he begged the sheriff for no more trouble.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:05.220
Teasle, driven to rage by the loss of his
friend, continued the fight, as Rambo incapacitated

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.690
his deputies in the woods.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.819
The National Guard arrived to help with the
search, and with them came Col. Trautman,

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:12.340
Rambo's former commanding officer.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.109
"I didn't come here to rescue Rambo from you.

00:02:15.109 --> 00:02:18.090
I came here to rescue you from him."

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:21.700
With the manhunt ramping up, the National
Guard troops went as far as blowing up an

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.930
abandoned mine to try to kill Rambo, but he
escaped into the town of Hope in pursuit of

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:26.930
Teasle.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.319
Trautman intervened and tried to convince
Rambo to surrender Rambo causing Rambo to

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:31.629
break down in tears.

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:35.370
Weeping and grieving, the veteran poured out
all the horrors he'd experienced during and

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.540
after the war.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.370
With Trautman's help, Rambo surrendered to
the authorities peacefully, and the great

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.440
warrior was ultimately sentenced to hard labor
in prison.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.349
Rambo spent the next four years in prison,
but that all changed when Col. Trautman returned

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:50.920
and offered him a presidential pardon and
his freedom.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:55.189
In exchange, Rambo would have to assist in
an operation to confirm reports of American

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.000
prisoners still being held in Vietnam, under
the supervision of Marshall Murdock.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.880
Rambo reluctantly agreed to this, but the
mission was rocky from the start.

00:03:02.889 --> 00:03:06.930
When Rambo spotted an American prisoner tied
up out in the open, he disobeyed orders and

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:07.930
rescued him.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:12.470
In the ensuing battle, Rambo destroyed a Vietnamese
gunboat and asked for extraction by American

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.470
forces.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.659
Murdock, fearing a scandal if the American
public found out about the remaining prisoners

00:03:16.659 --> 00:03:21.109
being left in Vietnam, left Rambo to be captured
by the Vietnamese and their Russian allies.

00:03:21.109 --> 00:03:24.400
Of course, Rambo ultimately escaped and freed
all the prisoners at the camp.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.639
When he returned to the American base with
the POWs, Rambo immediately made for Murdock's

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.880
office and machine-gunned his entire command
center in classic Rambo fashion.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.960
"AHHHHHHHH"

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.120
Then he went after Murdock, who'd left him
to die.

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:45.280
Trautman intervened and asked Rambo to walk
away and take his government pardon.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.209
Rambo, once again feeling betrayed by his
country's treatment of its soldiers, spared

00:03:49.209 --> 00:03:52.320
Murdock's life, but he didn't return to America.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.640
Three years after things went crazy in Vietnam,
Col. Trautman tracked down Rambo, who was

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.379
living in a kind of self-imposed exile in
Thailand.

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:03.690
Trautman asked Rambo for help in a CIA mission
to provide aid to Afghan fighters battling

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:04.830
the Soviets.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:09.060
Rambo declined, but when Trautman was captured
in Afghanistan, Rambo decided to embark on

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.120
a rescue mission.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.170
He headed over to Afghanistan to infiltrate
the Soviet base where Trautman was being held.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:18.700
He was able to rescue Trautman, but Soviet
Colonel Zaysen launched a pursuit, determined

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.890
to kill Rambo and Trautman both.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:25.480
After commandeering a Soviet tank, Rambo killed
Zaysen in the world's most epic game of chicken.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.690
With the battle won, Rambo and Trautman left
Afghanistan together, and Rambo ultimately

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:31.300
returned to isolation in Thailand.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.389
Around 20 years passed after the incident
in Afghanistan, and during all that time,

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:40.470
John Rambo managed to maintain his quiet life
in Thailand, earning a small living by catching

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.850
and selling snakes and transporting people
on his boat.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:46.780
But that all changed when a group of missionaries
from Colorado asked if he would take them

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.500
into Burma to provide humanitarian aid.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.500
Rambo was reluctant.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.030
“He’s like, ‘It’s a war zone up there.’”

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:56.450
But he agreed after one of the missionaries,
Sarah Miller, convinced him that they could

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:57.450
make a difference.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:00.220
“And he’s like, ‘You bringin’ any
weapons?’”

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:04.100
Rambo dropped the missionaries off in Burma,
only to later be approached by their minister,

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:07.640
who informed them of their capture by government
soldiers amid a mass slaughter.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:11.760
A big softie at heart, Rambo agreed to aide
a group of mercenaries hired by the church

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.440
to rescue the missionaries.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.560
And obviously, things got super bloody.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.850
In the middle of a fierce firefight, Rambo
pretty much single-handedly rescued the mercenaries

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:23.160
and the missionaries from essentially every
bad guy in Burma.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:27.090
After rescuing Sarah, Rambo took her message
of kindness to heart, and he returned home

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.280
to Arizona to visit his father for the first
time in many years.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.430
Rambo: Last Blood will pick up roughly a decade
after the events of Rambo, and while the film

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.750
hasn't been released yet, we do know a few
things about the plot.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.100
Rambo seems to have stayed in Arizona, and
he's made at least some kind of peace with

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.490
his existence there.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:47.920
Last Blood will feature Rambo's niece in peril
after she's abducted by a Mexican cartel.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:51.710
In an effort to get her back at all costs,
Rambo will revisit his old combat skills one

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:54.450
last time, heading into Mexico to battle the
cartel.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:58.570
We don't yet know exactly how that will unfold,
how much we'll learn about Rambo's home and

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:02.200
family life, or how well he's dealing with
his past trauma, but we do know two things

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.200
for sure.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.320
First, Rambo: Last Blood will hit theaters
on September 20, 2019.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:09.090
Second, there will definitely be some more
blood.

